1.5  "Personal Use" means use by one natural person, for that person's own
     purposes, where the use is not Commercial Use. Personal Use includes private
     study, experimentation, hobby projects, and personal projects that are not
     carried on for profit or commercial advantage.

1.6  "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software:

     (a) by, for, or on behalf of a legal entity of any kind, including a
         company, partnership, sole trader business, government body, or
         not-for-profit entity;

     (b) in the course of paid work, employment, contracting, consulting, or
         freelancing, whether or not the Software is used on the resulting
         deliverable directly;

     (c) to produce, maintain, operate, or support any product, service, or
         system that is sold, licensed, or otherwise commercially exploited; or

     (d) by more than one natural person.

     Use is Commercial Use if any one of (a) to (d) applies. Revenue is not the
     test: an employee using the Software on their employer's work is Commercial
     Use even if that particular project earns nothing.

1.7  "Commercial Licence" means a licence granted by us under clause 3 or 3A,
     covering a stated number of Seats for a stated term. A Commercial Licence
     may be granted at no charge under clause 3A.

1.8  "Seat" means one named natural person authorised to use the Software under a
     Commercial Licence. Seats are named, not concurrent. A Seat may be
     transferred to a replacement person if the original person ceases to require
     it, but may not be shared or rotated between people to serve more users than
     Seats purchased.

1.9  "Early Access" means the period, beginning on the date of this version and
     ending as set out in clause 3A.3, during which we grant Commercial Licences
     at no charge.

